  "checked": "2026-10-05",
  "notes": "DreamHack Stockholm is a gaming/esports festival rather than a classic guest-signing convention; the homepage itself only calls out two headline acts (bbno$ performing live; hololive hosting livestreams/meet-and-greets). Recheck pass (2026-10-05): the site's own 'Creators' nav tab leads to a dedicated Creator Hub page (dreamhack.com/stockholm/creator-hub/) naming 42 individual streamers/influencers accepted into the 2026 Creator Program (each card tagged '_2026', with Twitch/TikTok/YouTube/Instagram/X handles) -- these were missing from the original pass entirely. The Cosplay page (.../cosplay/) separately names 3 Cosplay Judges (Nukleara, Keksballs, Kuroru) and a 'Presented By' roster of 79 more creator-program streamers skewed toward cosplay content, 7 of whom also appear on the Creator Hub page (picked once, from the Creator Hub file, per the one-guest-one-pick rule) -- the other 72 plus the 3 judges are picked from the cosplay file. All ~117 added guests are cat 'creator' (or 'cosplay' for the judges); none have a fuller bio on these cards beyond their handle and platform icons, so known-for records the platforms shown. The separate Artist Alley page (.../artist-alley/) was also checked and correctly excluded: its ~83 tiles are vendor booths with Booth-ID tags (independent merch/craft sellers), which RESEARCH.md's rule explicitly skips as 'vendors'/'artist-alley tables', not announced guests -- confirmed by zero name overlap with the Creator Hub / Cosplay rosters. The Creator Program application page itself (.../creator-program/) is a generic 'apply here' page (applications closed Sept 30) with no additional names."
